# Default build-context filter for any `docker build` rooted at the repo.
#
# BuildKit looks for `.dockerignore` in the build-context directory; for the
# canonical NestJS template at `infra/docker/nestjs.Dockerfile` we pass the
# repo root as context, so this is the file Docker reads.
#
# Per-Dockerfile overrides are possible by placing `<dockerfile>.dockerignore`
# at the context root (BuildKit only). Add one when a service genuinely needs
# a different filter — most won't.

# Dependency caches — re-installed inside the deps stage from pnpm-lock.yaml
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store

# Build artefacts — compiled inside the builder stage
**/dist
**/build
**/out
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Generated Prisma clients (TS-502). Excluded for two reasons, both load-bearing:
#   1. The client embeds a platform-specific query-engine binary. A developer's
#      tree carries the Windows/macOS engine, and shipping that into an alpine
#      image is at best dead weight and at worst the only engine present.
#   2. Excluding it forces the builder stage to run `prisma generate` itself,
#      so the image is always built from `schema.prisma` rather than from
#      whatever happened to be on the machine that ran `docker build`.
# It is gitignored too, so on a clean CI checkout it never existed anyway —
# which is exactly the case this must not silently depend on.
**/prisma/generated

# Test outputs
**/coverage
**/coverage-integration
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/.nyc_output

# Source-control metadata — never needed inside the image
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# Local-only environment files (CLAUDE.md §3.5, §17.12)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Husky / lint-staged config — only relevant pre-commit
.husky

# Misc tooling output
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*

# Docs and trackers — no place in a runtime image
docs
PRD.md
PDD.md
CLAUDE.md
Pending_tasks.md
Completed_tasks.md
README.md
*.md
!apps/*/README.md
!packages/*/README.md
!infra/docker/README.md
